cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cite VitalRoute as below when referencing this software."
title: "VitalRoute: Vitality-Driven Adaptive Training for Imbalanced and Scarce Classification Tasks"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-05-30
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/alirazaanis/vitalroute"
abstract: >
  VitalRoute is a task-aware training controller that monitors four internal
  stress signals (stasis, weak weights, weak input, saturation) in neural
  network hidden units and uses a composite vitality score to automatically
  drive class-aware oversampling, label-free transfer parent selection, and
  per-layer learning rate dampening — all selected by a single adaptive router
  that reads only the shape of the training set.
keywords:
  - imbalanced learning
  - neural network health
  - adaptive training
  - dead neurons
  - class sampling
  - transfer learning
  - PyTorch
  - machine learning
authors:
  - name: "VitalRoute Contributors"
